            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Total submission, reverence, and the attribution of ultimate worth and glory to God, representing the surrender of the believer's entire life and will.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"John 4:23-24\",\"Romans 12:1\",\"Psalm 95:6\",\"Revelation 4:10-11\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Idolatry or spiritual adultery when directed toward anything other than God.\",\"basis\":[\"Exodus 20:3-5\",\"Revelation 13:4-8\",\"Romans 1:25\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Liturgical or ritual observance, focusing on the physical acts and communal gatherings of believers.\",\"basis\":[\"Hebrews 10:25\",\"Colossians 3:16\",\"1 Corinthians 14:26\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The eschatological harmony and ultimate submission of all creation at the end of the age.\",\"basis\":[\"Philippians 2:10-11\",\"Revelation 5:13-14\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"While 'worship' is a practical element of Christian liturgy, its theological and symbolic essence is overwhelmingly understood to transcend musical or ritual acts, representing instead a comprehensive posture of heart and life-surrender to the Creator.\"}",
